# Translations

Every new word or phrase shown on iPhone or Apple Watch must be translation-supported.

- Put copy in `i18n/locales/{en,fr,es,ko,de}.json` under the same key in every locale file. English is the default catalog.
- Render with `t('namespace.key')` from `useI18n()` (or `tRuntime` outside React). Interpolate with `{var}` placeholders, never concatenate user-facing sentences.
- Do not hardcode English (or any language) in screens, components, alerts, accessibility labels, or Watch UI.
- Plan, table, and session identifiers stay English in storage. Translate at display time and when syncing names/notes to Apple Watch.
- Watch chrome strings live in `targets/watch/l10n.swift` and must stay in sync with the `watch` keys in the JSON catalogs. Keep internal phase keys (`Hold`, `Rest`, `Breathe`) in English for logic; localize only the visible label.
- Supported languages: English (`en`, default), French (`fr`), Spanish (`es`), Korean (`ko`), German (`de`). Region-first device detection lives in `i18n/detect.ts`.
